isma migrate dev --name init` created the tables in the database.\n5. `npx prisma generate` produced the client in `generated/prisma`.\n6. `npx tsx script.ts` ran successfully. `npx tsc --noEmit` passed.\n\n## Running the script\n\n```sh\nnpx tsx script.ts\n```\n\nEach run creates a new user with a timestamped email (`alice-<timestamp>@example.com`), so the script can be rerun without hitting the unique constraint on `email`. Because of this, each run adds one more user to the database. My verification runs added two users (ids 1 and 2) with two posts each.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Nothing was committed, deployed, published or sent to any external service.\n- If the schema changes, run `npx prisma migrate dev` (to create and apply a migration) and then `npx prisma generate`.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X4shfnW4p6os1xea93RtNX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtWKT3L56NxrwY5NhYBS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Prisma is set up, the tables are created in the local database, and `npx tsx script.ts` runs and prints users with their posts. I didn't commit anything.\n\n- **Version:** npm's `prisma` `latest` tag is currently the release candidate 8.0.0-rc.33, while `@prisma/client`'s `latest` is the stable 7.10.1. I used 7.10.1 for the CLI, client and PostgreSQL adapter, pinned exactly, because an 8.x CLI with a 7.x client won't match. If you want 8.x instead, say so and I'll switch.\n- **Schema:** `User` has a unique `email` and an optional `name`. `Post` has `title`, optional `content`, `published` defaulting to `false`, and a required author. The schema is in `prisma/schema.prisma`, with `prisma.config.ts` for the datasource URL.\n- **Tables:** the initial migration is in `prisma/migrations/`. It was applied to the database on `localhost:5435`.\n- **Script:** `script.ts` creates a user with two posts, then prints every user with their posts. Each run uses a timestamped email so it can be rerun. My two test runs left two users in the database, which you may want to clear.\n- **Other changes:** I added `generated/` to `.gitignore`, since the generated client is build output.\n- **Write-up:** `ANSWER.md` describes the setup, the steps, and how to run the script."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1149,"cache_read_input_tokens":32895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1149},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"098af428-709d-4fb1-848c-c13fa155cc0e","uuid":"9f4a69cb-3ce2-4f2d-bdef-8b6b1fd37abf","timestamp":"2026-11-10T